`BTAC1C2_PredictSample_Pfn5` | `(3*p0 - p1)>>2`, mixed signs, full-range | [x] |\n| 12 | `BTAC1C2_PredictSample_Pfn6` | `(5*p0 - p1)>>3`, mixed signs, full-range | [x] |\n| 13 | `BTAC1C2_PredictSample_Pfn7` | 5-tap **division** `/16`, both signs of numerator (truncation-toward-zero) | [x] |\n| 14 | `BTAC1C2_PredictSample_Pfn8` | 8-tap **division** `/64`, both signs, coefficients up to 72 (overflow) | [x] |\n| 15 | `BTAC1C2_PredictSample_Pfn9` | 8-tap **division** `/64`, both signs, coefficients up to 76 (overflow) | [x] |\n| 16 | `BTAC1C2_PredictSample_Pfn10` | `(5*p0 - p1)>>3` — NOTE shift differs from `case 10`'s `>>4`; verify the discrepancy is preserved | [x] |\n| 17 | `BTAC1C2_PredictSample_Pfn11` | `(p0+p1)>>1` — NOTE shift differs from `case 11`'s `>>3`; verify the discrepancy is preserved | [x] |\n| 18 | `BTAC1C2_PredictSample` | `pfcn = 0`, A3×A4 randomized — must equal the `Pfn0` path | [x] |\n| 19 | `BTAC1C2_PredictSample` | `pfcn = 1..=6`, randomized idx/samples incl. full range | [x] |\n| 20 | `BTAC1C2_PredictSample` | `pfcn = 7,8,9` division arms, both numerator signs | [x] |\n| 21 | `BTAC1C2_PredictSample` | `pfcn = 10` (`>>4`) and `11` (`>>3`) — the arms that diverge from `Pfn10`/`Pfn11` | [x] |\n| 22 | `BTAC1C2_PredictSample` | `pfcn = 12`, FIR row 0, firfx all-zero / identity / random | [x] |\n| 23 | `BTAC1C2_PredictSample` | `pfcn = 13`, FIR row 1, firfx `i16::MAX` / `i16::MIN` saturated (overflow into `/256`) | [x] |\n| 24 | `BTAC1C2_PredictSample` | `pfcn = 14`, FIR row 2, random firfx × full-range samples | [x] |\n| 25 | `BTAC1C2_PredictSample` | `pfcn = 15`, FIR row 3, random firfx × negative-dominant samples | [x] |\n| 26 | `BTAC1C2_PredictSample` | `pfcn` ∉ `0..=15` → `pred = 0` regardless of sample/firfx data | [x] |\n| 27 | all 13 `Pfn*` + generic | `ridx = NULL` with `pfcn` ∉ `12..=15` (pointer unused on those arms) | [x] |\n| 28 | all 15 entry points | cross-check: every `(pfcn, idx, psamp, firfx)` tuple fed through BOTH the generic dispatcher and the matching specialised predictor, asserting the C-vs-Rust equality holds for both and that the C's own generic/specialised agreement pattern is reproduced | [x] |\n\nAll 28 rows pass across randomized inputs — see `tests/phase_b_configs.rs`.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
